{"reference":"2 Chronicles 32","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":32,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Recurring Pattern","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Hezekiah's illness and recovery are followed by pride, then by humility. This episode reflects a recurring pattern in Chronicles: seeking the LORD, praying, receiving prophetic instruction, or humbling oneself are set alongside the danger of turning away. The pattern helps readers see verses 24–26 as more than a private incident in Hezekiah's life; they also continue a recurring way the book portrays Judah's kings and people.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 32:24-26"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_032_5026cecdf9e90cfc7debfd84"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}